<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pan Africanist Congress of Azania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1959–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Pan Africanist Congress</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pan Africanist Congress (PAC) is a South African political party founded in 1959 by Robert Sobukwe and others who broke from the ANC to pursue an Africanist programme. Its campaign against the pass laws led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharpeville-massacre">Sharpeville massacre</a> of March 1960, after which it was banned. It was unbanned in February 1990, and its armed wing merged into the national army in 1994.</p></div>
